<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Bearing Man half year shr, div edges up.</title>
<headline>Bearing Man half year shr, div edges up.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Pre-excep shr, attrib (cts)</p>
<p>				  117	   vs 107</p>
<p>    Post-excep shr	  117	   vs 104</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 37	    vs 34</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   18.55	 vs 16.66</p>
<p>    Tax			 6.21	  vs 5.78</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   5.16	  vs 2.80</p>
<p>    Turnover		  170.23	vs 141.35</p>
<p>Div payable February 28</p>
<p>on register February 14</p>
<p>Full name: Bearing Man Ltd</p>
<p>    Exceptional items     nil	   vs 0.3 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - Bearing Man makes bearings, seals and power transmission products.</p>
<p>The firm said in a statement that it still expected to post earnings growth in the full year, but that a return to the higher levels of increase seen in recent years would have to await the advent of a more buoyant economy.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
